            <div xml:id="d405">

                <pb facs="0594" n="470" xml:id="pg470"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.48B/45: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Woods</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic">September 6,
                        1923</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 9—12:58 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Situation now thoroughly in hand. Five destroyers arrived from Chefoo and Admiral
                    Anderson on Flagship <hi rendition="#italic">Huron</hi> reached Yokohama this
                    afternoon. All American survivors Yokohama on ships and in safety. Embassy
                    evacuated 140 American tourists Tokio today on American destroyers and 21
                    British tourists.</p>
                <p>Relief ships being landed [<hi rendition="#italic">loaded?</hi>] in Tsingtau and
                    Manila. Arrival of fleet dispels danger of hunger among Americans.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Woods</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
